*.png
!nikxel_avatar.png
!sprites.png
.DS_Store
/tmp/
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Google OAuth. The real ones live in ~/.nikxel/, but a copy of the downloaded
# client JSON often sits in the working directory while setting it up -- this
# makes sure `git add .` can never publish it.
google_creds.json
google_token.json

# Build output. These are regenerated by ./build.sh on every run, and tracking
# them breaks the documented update path: a user who has built locally has a
# dirty working tree, so `git pull` refuses as soon as a commit touches the
# binary -- "your local changes would be overwritten". The committed copy was
# also permanently stale, so anyone who downloaded the repo and double-clicked
# the app silently ran an old version.
Nikxel.app/Contents/MacOS/Nikxel
Nikxel.app/Contents/_CodeSignature/

# Windows (Electron) app
!windows/resources/*.png
windows/node_modules/
windows/dist/
windows/release/
